Embedding threads per worker from the setting EMBEDDING_THREADS

Each uvicorn worker creates its query-embedding model at import with fastembed's
defaults: ONNX Runtime starts one intra-op thread per core and pins them to
cores 1..n-1, the same cores in every worker (measured in the modama search
stack on 8 vCPUs, 6 workers: 25 threads per worker, 7 pinned one each to CPUs
1 to 7). A setting `embedding_threads` (EMBEDDING_THREADS) passes fastembed's
`threads`, which sets intra_op_num_threads explicitly, so that ONNX Runtime
pins nothing. Unset, nothing changes. Embedding one query of tens of tokens
needs no more than one thread per worker.

Against the image ghcr.io/eosc-data-commons/data-commons-search:0.10.2 with
0001 applied; modama search stack, change cpu-budget (design D5, D9).

